<title>HONG KONG: Lehman sees SHK Prop at HK$110 within yr.</title>
<headline>Lehman sees SHK Prop at HK$110 within yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers Hong Kong sees Sun Hung Kai Properties Ltd trading at HK$110 within 12 months, senior investment analyst Michael Leary told a media briefing on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;It's a HK$110 stock in our view,&quot; Leary said.</p>
<p>He said positive factors included the company's large landmark, projected earnings growth of 22 percent in each of 1997 and 1998 and the fact that it had capital of HK$10 billion to increase its landbank.</p>
<p>The stock rose 75 H.K. cents to HK$89.00 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6352</p>
